  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 238 AM EDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nThe long term bring more fairly nondescript weather characterized by \ncontinued dry conditions and some fluctuation in temperatures. \nStarting with the weekend, a CAD setup will be in place across the \nregion, providing a renewed push of cooler weather. This cooler \nnortheast flow courtesy of surface high situated across the \nnortheastern US will keep highs largely in the 60s to low 70s \nthrough the weekend and lows back into the 40s areawide.\n\nBy early next week, the surface high will settle into the Southeast, \nkeeping things dry. Temperatures will be on a gradual warming trend \nthrough midweek, though staying largely seasonal. By this point, \nthere are hints of a pattern change as the upper low over the \nSouthwest US lifts into the Plains, flattening the persistent \nridge over the central US. While this may foretell a more active \npattern thereafter, things still look to stay dry locally through \nthe end of next week. Ensemble guidance currently largely holds \noff any substantive increase in rain chances until we start to \nhead into November.",
